Mastodon API importer
=====================

This is an importer for microblogging servers exposing the Mastodon API. This
includes Mastodon as well as Pleroma.

It imports the account's own statuses as children of the root's "statuses"
node, keyed by their ActivityPub IDs (URIs). A status's node, of camliNodeType
"mastodon:status", has its ActivityPub ID as activityPubId (and its web page's
URL as url); its text as written, from the server's /api/v1/statuses/:id/source
(Mastodon 3.5 and later), as its content and title; its HTML as the server
rendered it, as contentHTML, unless that's just the text's paragraphs and
lines; and its visibility, content warning, language, link preview, and the
URI of the status it replies to (and the server's IDs of it and its author).
Its media are its children, such as camliPath:image1, of camliNodeType
"mastodon:image" (or "mastodon:video", "mastodon:gifv", "mastodon:audio"), with
the file as camliContent, alt text as description, and a video's preview image
as camliContentImage.

Others' statuses that the account boosted, favourited, bookmarked or replied to
are children of "linkedStatuses", of camliNodeType "mastodon:linkedStatus",
alike but with their text from their HTML, and their authors. The account's
boosts, favourites and bookmarks are children of "reblogs", "favourites" and
"bookmarks", of camliNodeType "mastodon:reblog" (and so on), whose camliContent
is the status's node, its own or another's. Its profile is the root's
"profile", of camliNodeType "mastodon:profile", with its avatar as
camliContentImage, its header image as header, and its fields; the accounts it
follows are children of "following", of camliNodeType "mastodon:follow", whose
camliContent is the account's profile, of camliNodeType
"mastodon:linkedProfile", a child of "accounts". Finding the
statuses replied to needs Mastodon 4.3 or later.

Each page of a list is stored with one claim: a multi claim of all its items'
changes, their new children's camliPaths and media's included, after one
upload of the permanodes they lack. An incremental run stops at each list's
first page that's unchanged, and doesn't fetch the text or media it already has
of a status, unless the status has been edited since. Set
PERKEEP_MASTODON_FULL_IMPORT=1 to look at all statuses.

The API's rate limit, by default 300 calls every 5 minutes, is shared with the
account's other apps. A run leaves a fifth of it for them, waiting for the rest
of the window when it's used the rest, so a first run of an account of many
statuses, which fetches each one's text, takes a while: about 240 statuses
every 5 minutes.
